roughly 9% of the rubbish we believe  could be recycled instead so let's take  a closer look at how to use the  recycling bin  everything you put into the bin should  be clean and loose not in a bag and lids  and tops from bottles and jars should be  removed if they're plastic they should  go in the rubbish any scrap metal can be  recycled at Southbrook resource recovery  Park other items that can't be accepted  include broken glass milk or juice  cartons also known as tetrapack  polystyrene and soft plastics soft  plastics include anything you can easily  scrunch up into your hand this includes  bubble wrap food wrap chip packets and  plastic bags nappies should go on the  rubbish and food sword cardboard like  pizza boxes or napkins should go into  your organics bin for composting so what  should go into your recycling glass  bottles and jars bottles and containers  made from plastic type 1 through 7  tonnes cans and aerosols and loose clean  flat cardboard and paper to learn more  or to sign up for collection reminders  visit 1 a kediri govt tnz forward slash  rethink rubbish
 

